<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21275] sanity test_64f: grants mismatch after second remount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21275</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_64f fails intermittently with:&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;buffered io, not write rpc|...&amp;gt;: grants mismatch: &amp;lt;got&amp;gt;, expected &amp;lt;expected&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The test remounts the client a second time ("Remount client to reset grant") and re-reads osc_tgt, but still compares check_grants against the init_grants it read after the first mount. The initial grant an OST hands out on a new connection isn't always the same, so the later checks compare against a stale value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: re-read initial_grant from the OSC import after the second remount_client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Earlier test_64f "grants mismatch" tickets (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13847" title="sanity test_64f: grants mismatch" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13847"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13847&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15704" title="sanity test_64f: buffered io, not write rpc: grants mismatch: 12656640, expected 4218880" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15704"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15704&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16541" title="sanity test_64f: buffered io, not write rpc: grants mismatch: 12656640, expected 4218880 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16541"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16541&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20699" title="sanity test_64f: direct io with grant allocation: grants mismatch: 126566400, expected 75362304" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20699"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20699&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) are all closed, and none of them describes this cause. test_64e has the same pattern: it remounts a second time and calls check_grants without re-reading init_grants.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;distro/arch&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;ldiskfs|zfs&amp;gt;</environment>
